# Add this line to the droplet's existing crontab (crontab -e) alongside
# everything else already there. No API key needed -- HRRR's own free
# GRIB2 distribution (AWS Open Data, falling back to NOMADS/Google) is
# unauthenticated.
#
# Every 6 hours at :30, 2.5h after each synoptic HRRR cycle's init time
# (00z/06z/12z/18z -> 02:30/08:30/14:30/20:30 UTC). Verified directly
# against AWS's HRRR bucket (Last-Modified on the actual F48 GRIB2 files,
# 8 consecutive cycles): every cycle's F48 posts remarkably consistently
# at ~1h44-47m after its nominal init time, so this leaves a ~45min
# cushion past that observed posting time for an occasional slow cycle --
# not the ~2.5-3h once assumed here (based on a comment in
# ../../tri-cities-7day-forecast/fetch_hrrr_smoke_forecast.py that turned
# out not to match this field's actual posting behavior). Re-verify with
# `curl -sSI https://noaa-hrrr-bdp-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/hrrr.<YYYYMMDD>/conus/hrrr.t<HH>z.wrfsfcf48.grib2`
# if NOAA's posting cadence ever seems to have changed.
# fetch_smoke.py's own select_latest_48h_run() falls back to the previous
# complete cycle if this one's still posting, so an occasional late run
# degrades gracefully rather than failing outright.

30 2,8,14,20 * * * /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/venv/bin/python3 /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/deploy/publish_smoke.py >> /opt/ingalls-weather-scripts/hrrr-smoke-chart/state/cron.log 2>&1
